      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the previous was `copy_stack_to_slots`, then it seems possible for this to produce different results (but with no actual consequence, I suppose?). The `copy_stack_to_slots` would be masked, so the thing that was on the stack will be a mix of actually-new values that were stored, and values that weren\u0027t written (due to masking). Without this optimization, we\u0027d emit `push_slots`, so we\u0027d get the real values in every lane (including masked lanes).\n\n... but I guess that\u0027s safe because we never really interleave mask changes with theses kinds of ops? eg, we wouldn\u0027t issue a push_slots, expecting to get a variable\u0027s contents on the stack, and then un-mask lanes? Eh, could that happen in the context of a loop with continues? Probably not.",
